{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider must not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before a conditional offer; afterwards it may consider only specified serious or recent convictions, after an individualized assessment and with appeal rights, and must not advertise a blanket criminal-record bar.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes; not a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applicants may be asked about certain drug-related convictions in federally assisted housing and about lifetime sex offender registration.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; inquiry into certain drug-related activity in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration is permitted.","penalty":"Up to $1,000 for a first violation, up to $5,000 for one prior violation within five years, and up to $10,000 for two or more prior violations within seven years; the director may order compliance measures and payment of up to $1,000 to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include criminal history review and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes; not a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Duty applies before the housing provider accepts an application fee.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require the applicant's rental application fee to be returned; violations are subject to the act's monetary penalties.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1)   Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal overturns a director's order that placed an applicant in its unit, the provider may evict that former applicant from the unit it owns because of the order, with at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director's order under section 12.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies only where the housing provider's successful appeal overturns the director's order placing the applicant in its unit.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Applies notwithstanding any provision of the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

